   "line": 8,
   "text": "The trouble is the edges: the block cuts a turn short, and the end arrows count in full. Lesson ten cured a sharp cut with a taper. Multiply the block by the [HH AA1 N] window, Hamming's cousin, fading to zero at both ends. The end arrows shrink, and the side lobe falls from twenty-two percent to two point seven. [surprise-oh] Now the faintest key scores nine point two, and a bar at five percent decodes every press.",
