   "line": 9,
   "text": "Why not a shorter block? At one twenty-eight, a loud one leaks sixty-one percent into the four's bin: the taper bought low side lobes with a main lobe twice as wide. Longer isn't the rule either: two twenty-four fails, two oh eight works. What counts is where the bins land. With loud keys ten times the faint, every neighbouring tone needs about one point seven five bins of room. Two fifty-six gives two point two six.",
